  "review": {
    "entityID": "person:abraham_58",
    "book": "ROM",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "What then will we say that Abraham, our forefather, has found according to the flesh?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:2 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For if Abraham was justified by works, he has something to boast about, but not toward God."
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:3 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For what does the Scripture say? “Abraham believed God, and it was accounted to him for righteousness.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:9 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Is this blessing then pronounced only on the circumcised, or on the uncircumcised also? For we say that faith was accounted to Abraham for righteousness."
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:12 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "He is the father of circumcision to those who not only are of the circumcision, but who also walk in the steps of that faith of our father Abraham, which he had in uncircumcision."
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:13 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For the promise to Abraham and to his offspring that he would be heir of the world wasn’t through the law, but through the righteousness of faith."
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 4:16 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For this cause it is of faith, that it may be according to grace, to the end that the promise may be sure to all the offspring, not to that only which is of the law, but to that also which is of the faith of Abraham, who is the father of us all."
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 9:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Neither, because they are Abraham’s offspring, are they all children. But, “your offspring will be accounted as from Isaac.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "ROM 11:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "I ask then, did God reject his people? May it never be! For I also am an Israelite, a descendant of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin."
      }
    ],
